  "notes": "Kuala Lumpur Kepong Berhad (KLK) — integrated palm oil producer with substantial downstream (oleochemicals) and property arms. Fiscal year ends September 30 (NOT calendar year). Quarters: 1Q = Oct-Dec, 2Q = Jan-Mar, 3Q = Apr-Jun, 4Q = Jul-Sep. ~285,000 ha (~705,000 acres) total planted area across Malaysia, Indonesia, Liberia, PNG. Four reportable IFRS 8 segments: Plantations (FFB/CPO/PK upstream), Manufacturing (oleochemicals + refining + kernel crushing — globally leading via KLK Oleo, Davos, Temix Oleo etc.), Property (KL East, Bandar Seri Coalfields), Investment Holding (treasury + corporate). Quarterly data from Bursa Malaysia Form 8 quarterly reports filed via KLK IR; annual data from FY2020-2024 annual reports (5-year financial summary table). Acres = planted ha × 2.47/1000. Net debt = total borrowings − cash & equivalents. KLK's reported revenue swings with palm + oleochemical pricing; FY22 was a peak (CPO RM5,800/MT avg) and FY24 saw normalization. Quarterly EBITDA = PBT + finance costs + depreciation/amortization where disclosed; some EBITDA values estimated from disclosed PBT trends.",
